00:04:53.979 --> 00:04:55.600
Wednesday prefers to do things alone.

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:56.600
I'll survive alone.

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:57.630
I always have.

00:04:57.630 --> 00:05:02.620
However, in the end, taking down the villainous
trio of Laurel, the Hyde and Crackstone was

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:06.080
something Wednesday simply couldn't do by
herself;

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:08.570
instead it required a team effort.

00:05:08.570 --> 00:05:12.970
This was predicted early on when she met Eugene
for the first time and he explained why he

00:05:12.970 --> 00:05:14.669
liked bees so much.

00:05:14.669 --> 00:05:16.600
They're nature's perfect community.

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:19.039
All working together to achieve a common goal.

00:05:19.039 --> 00:05:24.050
So, although Wednesday confronts Tyler alone,
it's one of her friends, Enid after wolfing

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:27.300
out who saves her just before he's about to
kill her.

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:32.070
Then when Wednesday tries to take down the
evil Crackstone, the villain smashes her sword

00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:37.470
to pieces with his magical staff and is about
to finish her off, but Bianca stabs him from

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:41.250
behind, which gives Wednesday just enough
time to grab a shard of the sword and this

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:45.009
time she stabs him in the heart, which as
her ancestor Goody explained…

00:05:45.009 --> 00:05:46.009
Crackstone must be stabbed through his black
heart.

00:05:46.009 --> 00:05:48.210
It is the only way he will be vanquished now
and forever.

00:05:48.210 --> 00:05:52.990
After Crackstone's demise, Laurel decides
to kill Wednesday herself, but this time it's

00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:56.729
her friend Eugene who stops Laurel when he
turns up with his bees.

00:05:56.729 --> 00:05:59.910
Wednesday's my only friend, and if she's in
trouble, I've got to help her.

00:05:59.910 --> 00:06:00.910
It's hive code.

00:06:00.910 --> 00:06:05.410
By the way, Wednesday taking an arrow to the
shoulder to save Xavier from Crackstone, mirrors

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:09.730
how he saved her from the falling gargoyle
in the first episode.

00:06:09.730 --> 00:06:14.740
The last few moments of the finale leave us
with some big questions for a potential Season

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:19.520
2, such as who is the mystery stalker sending
threatening texts to Wednesday?

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:23.230
Someone who might be antagonistic towards
her is the Siren guy, Kent.

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:28.630
He was in charge of sabotaging the other teams
during the Poe Cup race, however both Wednesday's

00:06:28.630 --> 00:06:33.130
net and Thing's punch to the face stopped
him, and he ended up getting the blame for

00:06:33.130 --> 00:06:34.669
queen bee Bianca losing.

00:06:34.669 --> 00:06:38.400
It was your job to help us win and she's never
lost.

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:42.530
Wednesday also made him look foolish in front
of the other Nightshades when she explained

00:06:42.530 --> 00:06:44.919
how she'd discovered their secret meeting
room.

00:06:44.919 --> 00:06:45.919
Then I solved the riddle.

00:06:45.919 --> 00:06:46.919
Wait, there's a riddle?

00:06:46.919 --> 00:06:47.970
I thought we just snapped twice.

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:49.810
Well, aren't you the brightest in the bunch?

00:06:49.810 --> 00:06:51.500
Seriously, even Kent is here?

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:53.250
How exclusive is this club?

00:06:53.250 --> 00:06:58.400
Alternately, it might be someone connected
to the MorningSong cult run by Bianca's mum.

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:02.539
It seemed like a weird subplot when this came
up, and I wonder whether it'll be explored

00:07:02.539 --> 00:07:04.210
further in Season 2.

00:07:04.210 --> 00:07:08.819
We are a personal development movement that
helps people take control of their lives.

00:07:08.819 --> 00:07:10.960
After you take control of their bank account.

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:15.810
Another possibility could be the mayor's son
Lucas, who got interested in MorningSong via

00:07:15.810 --> 00:07:19.229
a self-help app that Bianca's mum recommended
to him.

00:07:19.229 --> 00:07:21.870
His father was killed, presumably by Laurel.

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:26.680
And although he appears to regret the Carrie-style
stunt at the Rave'N, he and his two mates

00:07:26.680 --> 00:07:31.530
do have an antagonistic history with Wednesday
when she fought them after they harassed her

00:07:31.530 --> 00:07:33.240
at the coffee shop.

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:36.440
And the final shot of Season 1 has Tyler Hulking
out –

00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:41.099
or, rather, Hyding out –
which makes me wonder if Laurel is actually

00:07:41.099 --> 00:07:46.170
dead, or whether she's still alive and able
to trigger him to transform into a Hyde.

00:07:46.170 --> 00:07:50.400
She may still have some kind of connection
with Tyler, and so after he presumably breaks

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:54.580
out of the truck, he could go and find her
and together they could plot their revenge

00:07:54.580 --> 00:07:55.680
on Wednesday.

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:58.819
So, who do you think Wednesday's stalker could
be?

00:07:58.819 --> 00:08:01.389
And is Principal Weems really dead?

